     It is not gratuitous; it indicates a real problem.  The way version
3.1.* updates the existing scoreboard file in place--as opposed to 3.0pl*,
which created a new file and used that to replace the old one--will only
work correctly if the file has Stream_LF record format (as reported by
DIRECTORY/FULL).  If the record format is different, then attempts to
update the file with new entries will fail (maybe not all the time, but
I no longer remember the specific circumstances where it doesn't work).

     The simplest way to fix it is to use CONVERT/FDL to make a new copy
with the appropriate format, then replace the old copy.  It must end up
as file version 1 or NetHack will ignore it.

$ set default hackdir
$ convert/fdl=sys$input: record. *.*
file
 organization sequential
record
 format stream_lf
<ctrl/Z>
$ purge record.
$ rename record. *.*;1

     You should also apply the following patch to bones.c, recompile that
one file, and relink nethack.exe.  (Install.vms describes how to do this
in detail.)  Otherwise, the presence of some "bones" data files can cause
games to be arbitrarily terminated due to "trickery".  This particular
problem is VMS-specific (and was also present in 3.1.1; I'm not sure about
3.1.0), but applying this patch won't interfere with any other ports.
